ad/crawl/dicoms/dartmouth-phantoms/bids_test3 (create_sibling.py:242)\n\u003e \n\u003e initial workaround could be as simple as\n\u003e \n\u003e $\u003e git diff\n\u003e diff --git a/datalad/distribution/add_sibling.py b/datalad/distribution/add_sibling.py\n\u003e index aabe7e0..04d3c0e 100644\n\u003e --- a/datalad/distribution/add_sibling.py\n\u003e +++ b/datalad/distribution/add_sibling.py\n\u003e @@ -166,8 +166,7 @@ class AddSibling(Interface):\n\u003e                  if repos[repo_name]['url'].rstrip('/') != existing_url.rstrip('/') \\\n\u003e                          or (pushurl and existing_pushurl and\n\u003e                              repos[repo_name]['pushurl'].rstrip('/') !=\n\u003e -                                    existing_pushurl.rstrip('/')) \\\n\u003e -                        or (pushurl and not existing_pushurl):\n\u003e - ```\n\u003e                                  existing_pushurl.rstrip('/')):\n\u003e                conflicting.append(repo_name)\n\u003e   \n\u003e    if not force and conflicting:\n\u003e   ```\n\u003e \n\u003e but I think we should altogether not set those pushurls if == url. Agreed?\n\u003e \n\u003e —\n\u003e You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n\u003e https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/948, or mute the thread\n\u003e https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAIVH-QjWuVOWrDobLSIx_-Ot-I6hp-Jks5quqUbgaJpZM4KJGVQ\n\u003e .\n\n## \n\nMichael Hanke\nhttp://psychoinformatics.de","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475869627,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MjM0NDU4MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/948#issuecomment-252344581"},"message":"@bpoldrack working on this one or should I?","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480103807,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2Z